# Knowledge source requests for local testing (VS Code REST Client or JetBrains HTTP Client).
#
# Sign in first with auth.http (request 4) and create a bot with bots.http, in the
# same client. Every non-GET request needs an Origin equal to APP_URL.
# Sources are processed in the background: list them again after a moment to see
# queued → processing → ready (or failed with a reason).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api
@origin = http://localhost:3000
@botId = PASTE_BOT_ID_HERE
@sourceId = PASTE_SOURCE_ID_HERE

### Upload a file (PDF, DOCX, MD or TXT, up to 10 MB) — 201, status "queued"
POST {{baseUrl}}/bots/{{botId}}/sources/file
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=hovr

--hovr
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="faq.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

# FAQ

## Do you ship to Canada?

Yes. Orders to Canada arrive in 5 to 8 business days, and duties are paid at checkout.
--hovr--

### Add pasted text — 201, status "queued"
POST {{baseUrl}}/bots/{{botId}}/sources/text
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Payment methods",
  "text": "We accept Visa, Mastercard, Amex, PayPal and Apple Pay. We don't accept crypto."
}

### List the bot's sources with status, chunks and failure reasons
GET {{baseUrl}}/bots/{{botId}}/sources

### Wrong file type — 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/bots/{{botId}}/sources/file
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=hovr

--hovr
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="setup.exe"
Content-Type: application/octet-stream

nope
--hovr--

### Delete a source — 204 (its chunks and stored file go too)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/bots/{{botId}}/sources/{{sourceId}}
Origin: {{origin}}
